# Agent plates on books — full-perimeter deckle

**CRITICAL.** Whenever surfacing an agent on a Living Folio / book page (Clive study stage, teaching state, agent-interaction comps, cast plates on parchment):

1. **All four sides dissolve.** Top, bottom, left, and right must use the same papery deckle / charcoal dissolve into the page. A hard horizontal (or vertical) cutoff through the figure is a defect — especially a ruler-line bottom above body copy.
2. **Welcome / copy is not the plate edge.** Text below the plate sits on parchment *after* the dissolve finishes. Never use a hard crop to "make room" for Welcome.
3. **Still and video share one mask.** The matte wraps the plate container so poster and MP4 get the same edge (`mask-image` luminance matte, or a vignette baked into a transparent plate). Do not soft-`radial-gradient` alone — that reads as blur, not paper.
4. **House assets (Clive study):** Curated MP4s stay primary (`CliveVideoStage` + `video-reactions.ts`). REF supplies the **border only**. Teaching (left): luminance matte on `.study-stage__clive-plate` (`clive-folio-deckle-v9-4k.png`, white=show, 4096×3020) + ink (`clive-folio-deckle-ink-v9-4k.png`), aspect `1024 / 755`. Interaction (right): `clive-folio-deckle-interaction-v9-4k.png` + `clive-folio-deckle-ink-interaction-v9-4k.png` (4096×2518, aspect `4096 / 2518`), scoped under `[data-folio-state="interaction"]`. Ink must sit *outside* the mask or the rim gets clipped. Use `mask-mode: luminance` (Safari ignores alpha mattes). Do **not** replace the video bank with a REF still.
5. **Taste gate.** Kathryn / Tara-Lee own visual finish; do not declare a new matte final without their eye when the look changes.

Canonical note also lives in `website/docs/chapter1-craft-build-pack.md` (ground truth).
